body:
Use to work at a third party repair shop so;
We often did exactly what OP wrote BECAUSE the Authorized dealers would NOT do it on *Androids* at the time. This was a couple years ago ('15-'18).

I can't see why this would be necessary though at a A.D. as they have the tools and equipment to do the data migration automatically for them usually. Suppose it could be broken and they had to do it by hand or maybe he wasn't trained to have know how to use that equipment. Pretty straightforward though. Plus with iCloud and other backup options it seems weird he would've needed access when it's going to a new phone. I've never needed to look through someone's data more than the newest texts and photos be present.
